{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793305899,"nonce":"mShsfAFWOmDpbA178s21C4ghTgc=","title":"Priority 4 in the WASM compilation-speed effort. Related: 77aa1c9 (host export/root discussion), 6fb5fe6 (WASM module size), 3b7fa54 (shard loading), 8b12bc8 (LLVM artifact reuse).","message":"AOT currently lowers every bytecode function and emits registries that retain their addresses. The diagnostic reachable::analyze explicitly excludes reflection roots; its live set cannot safely authorize deletion. WindowPage spends roughly 6 s emitting LLVM IR before backend work.\n\nDefine and test a sound root/edge policy for entry points, reflection-visible classes and methods, dynamic/virtual calls, closures, host exports, function tables and native callbacks. Root sets and type/function registries must agree. Then prevent proven-unused functions and unnecessary call-signature trampolines from reaching LLVM, preserving conservative fallback for unknown dynamic uses.\n\nAcceptance: reflection/closure/host-entry regressions, disabled-versus-enabled output behavior on native and both WASM modes, complete Ashui browser runs, and cold/warm/edit timing, RSS, body-count and module-size measurements. Do not repurpose the current diagnostic analysis as a deletion list without covering its omissions. No percentage gain claimed before measurements.","files":null}]}